# Committed on purpose. This holds no secret - it is the site's own public
# address, and it needs to be identical in two places that cannot import from
# each other: index.html (static markup, substituted by Vite as %VITE_SITE_URL%)
# and src/app/head.ts (runtime, read as import.meta.env.VITE_SITE_URL).
#
# One value, one file. A custom domain later is a change here and nowhere else,
# and Netlify can override it per-deploy with an environment variable of the
# same name without touching the repo at all.
#
# The build FAILS if this is missing or is not an absolute https URL - an
# og:image with a relative or half-substituted URL is worse than no card at
# all, and it is exactly the kind of thing nobody notices until someone shares
# a link. See vite/plugins/index-html.ts.
VITE_SITE_URL=https://patchbay-tools.netlify.app
